Bug 1965151 - Don't let Opaque Response Blocking block calendar requests after a cross-origin redirect. r=tobyp

Calendar HTTP requests use a content principal, so that different users on the
same server get separate connections, and were sent as no-cors TYPE_OTHER
loads. After a redirect to another origin the response is opaque, and ORB then
blocks it, e.g. a text/calendar response with "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff".
That made it impossible to subscribe to calendars behind such a redirect, like
an http URL that redirects to https, or public Google calendars at
www.google.com/calendar/ical/... which redirect to calendar.google.com.

Load them like a system XHR instead, which ORB exempts, and keep the content
principal and its origin attributes.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335055

diff --git a/calendar/base/modules/utils/calProviderUtils.sys.mjs b/calendar/base/modules/utils/calProviderUtils.sys.mjs
--- a/calendar/base/modules/utils/calProviderUtils.sys.mjs
+++ b/calendar/base/modules/utils/calProviderUtils.sys.mjs
@@ -91,15 +91,17 @@ export var provider = {
       ? null
       : Services.scriptSecurityManager.createContentPrincipal(aUri, originAttributes);
     const channel =
       aExistingChannel ||
+      // Load like a system XHR, so that Opaque Response Blocking doesn't block
+      // responses after a cross-origin redirect.
       Services.io.newChannelFromURI(
         aUri,
         null,
         principal,
         null,
-        Ci.nsILoadInfo.SEC_ALLOW_CROSS_ORIGIN_SEC_CONTEXT_IS_NULL,
-        Ci.nsIContentPolicy.TYPE_OTHER
+        Ci.nsILoadInfo.SEC_ALLOW_CROSS_ORIGIN_INHERITS_SEC_CONTEXT,
+        Ci.nsIContentPolicy.TYPE_XMLHTTPREQUEST
       );
     let httpchannel = channel.QueryInterface(Ci.nsIHttpChannel);
 
     httpchannel.setRequestHeader("Accept", "text/xml", false);
